    <summary>Local-first notes, tasks and time tracking with SAP and Jira booking, calendar and optional AI.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[Arcalo is a desktop app for Markdown notes that link to each other, tasks, daily notes and time tracking.

## Features

- Markdown notes with `[[wiki links]]`, backlinks, tags, tables, tasks and a page tree; imports an Obsidian vault and exports everything back to Markdown files.
- Time tracking in the note: type `/time NP-8801/1020 2.5h` to book on an SAP PS activity or `/time 1h PROJ-123` to book on a Jira issue. The weekly timesheet exports to SAP CATS, Jira, CSV or JSON.
- Jira Cloud and Server / Data Center: your issues and saved searches, offline, with worklogs.
- Meetings from Outlook and other calendars (ICS) next to the booked time.
- Voice notes transcribed on your computer with whisper.cpp.
- An assistant on your own AI provider (LiteLLM, OpenAI-compatible, Azure OpenAI) or a local model (Ollama).
- All data stays in one database on your computer, with no account and no telemetry. Git sync and backups are optional.
- English and German interface.

## Package notes

The package runs the official per-user installer (`Arcalo_<version>_x64-setup.exe`) from the GitHub release silently. Arcalo is installed for the account Chocolatey runs as, into `%LOCALAPPDATA%`. The app can also update itself; `choco upgrade arcalo` installs the new version over it.
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/MouseWerk/Arcalo/releases/tag/v1.11.0</releaseNotes>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
